From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ats0c <ats0c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:05:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos9830: cap big cluster at 2.21 GHz

The Mongoose M5 cores spend most of their power in the top frequency
steps for little extra performance.  Lower the big cluster cpufreq
domain's max-freq from 2730000 to 2210000: exynos-acme drops the higher
entries from the frequency table, so no PM QoS request, governor boost
or user limit can select them.

2210000 is also the highest big frequency whose MIF constraint is
2288000 instead of 2535000, so memory can stay one step lower under big
cluster load.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9830.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9830.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9830.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9830.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9830.dts
@@ -863,7 +863,7 @@
 			dm-type = <DM_CPU_CL2>;
 			need-awake;
 
-			max-freq = <2730000>;
+			max-freq = <2210000>;
 			min-freq = <546000>;
 
 			/* PM QoS Class ID*/
-- 
2.43.0

